GRA-25: hgraphOrderCp()/hmeshOrderCp() leak the coarse column block tree when the compressed ordering fails
(and PS2-G15-1: hgraphOrderCc() leaves uninitialized tree cells on failure -> invalid free in orderExit()).
Files: dbl2.grf (two copies of a doubled 8x8 grid: compressible, 2 components; generated by the python snippet in the
session), dbl.msh (small2.msh with every node doubled: compressible mesh), leak.c (orders then scrubs the stack so
that LeakSanitizer does not see stale pointers).
Build: gcc -O0 -g -fsanitize=address,undefined -I<tree>/include leak.c -o leak -L<tree>/lib -lscotch -lscotcherr -lz -lm -lpthread
Run (LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<tree>/lib UBSAN_OPTIONS=print_stacktrace=1 (pristine tree: INFRA/asan; patched: $WORK/build or $WORK/build64), leak detection ON, SCOTCH_PTHREAD_NUMBER=1):
  ./leak g dbl2.grf 'c{rat=0.9,cpr=o{strat=b{cmin=0,strat=s}},unc=s}'       # GRA-25 graph
  ./leak m dbl.msh  'c{rat=0.9,cpr=n{sep=h,ole=b{cmin=0,strat=s},ose=s},unc=s}' # GRA-25 mesh twin
  ./leak g dbl2.grf 'o{strat=b{cmin=0,strat=s}}'                            # PS2-G15-1
Pristine: graph: "Direct leak of 56 byte(s) ... hgraphOrderCc <- hgraphOrderSt <- hgraphOrderCp" (the coarse tree);
mesh: "Direct leak of 72 byte(s) ... hmeshOrderNd <- hmeshOrderSt <- hmeshOrderCp"; third: ASan BUS/invalid free in
orderExit2 from SCOTCH_graphOrderExit (uninitialized cblktab cells, 0xbe fill pattern).
Patched (0003 + 0004): all three print the strategy error only, "order ret=1", no leak, no crash.
